#!/bin/sh
###################################################################################
# @file        DeleteRecordByIP.sh
# @brief       Deletes a specific DNS A record matching a given domain and IP address.
# @author      Peter Winter
# @date        10/11/2026
# @version     1.0
#
# @details     This script parses a target Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) to extract
#              the zone apex, queries the Linode API to find the domain tracking ID, isolates
#              the explicit record ID associated with the target IP address, and issues a 
#              DELETE request to remove the entry.
#
# @param       $1  [Required] The target Fully Qualified Domain Name or URL string.
# @param       $2  [Required] The destination tracking node IPv4/IPv6 target address to drop.
#
# @env         HOME                Path to the stand-alone environment framework directory.
#
# @dependencies
#              - /home/homedir.dat configuration file tracking active base home path.
#              - ExtractConfigValue.sh configuration variable extraction utility.
#              - external dependencies: cat, echo, cut, curl, jq, test
#
# @security    
#              - Hardens executable locations (/bin, /usr/bin) to negate path hijacking.
#              - Scopes and purges sensitive tokens (TOKEN) tightly inside execution tracks.
#              - Protects dynamic JSON queries from code parameter injection tracking bugs.
#
# @exit        0  Success: Target DNS record successfully dropped via API track.
# @exit        1  Failure: Missing context paths, input parameter errors, or API failures.
